// Act I — the Desktop (the living room): the summons, Computer Bingo,
// the first program sent to the Internet, and Trabolta coming online.
//
// The set pieces have no program bound: they are reached from main.loom's
// story rules, so every line lands in the Desktop's room on every phone
// (and reads like captions for what Clippy is saying in the room). The
// physical business — the cards, the ribbon, the drag to the Tube — is
// the performers'; the phones carry the rules and the reveal. No
// featured program ever has a line (they are guests; see cast/featured.loom).
//
// The prop beats at the end (`The Screensaver`, `The Router`) are scanned
// one program at a time, so their lines are private to that program.

// C1 / V1 — `call_to_the_desktop`.
== Call To The Desktop
  setting: The Desktop

Every screen in the house says the same thing. An Antivirus walks the halls, sweeping programs toward the living room.

// V2 — `start_the_bingo` (Clippy Instructions 1/X).
== Computer Bingo
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Task Manager, Adobe Acrobat, Recycling Bin

Clippy: Hello! Hello, everyone! Welcome to the computer! We're so glad you've decided to join us for a special fundraiser party to restore the sign at Maps And Ducks.
Clippy: I'm Clippy, the official Office Assistant with Maps and Ducks. If anyone needs Help With That, I'll be available.
// DRAFT w18b (R17): the owner joins by video conference later.
Clippy: Jean Trabolta will be joining us later in the night! He'll be joining by video conference, because we are all people who have become computer programs, but he has ALWAYS been a computer program.
Clippy: He may or may not have already shared with you that he is an AI, but rest assured: he is the true owner of Maps and Ducks, and he is excited to lead you through Jean Trabolta's Scavenger Hunt!
Clippy: Please welcome your hosts! Task Manager, who keeps things running!
Task Manager: Hello. Per the agenda: hello. I will be keeping things running.
Clippy: Adobe Acrobat, who will assist with documents and printing!
Adobe Acrobat: You are all PORTABLE DOCUMENTS of pure POTENTIAL, and I love you. Printing is extra.
Clippy: And the Recycling Bin, responsible for hygiene and maintenance!
Recycling Bin: Programs. Disk Cleanup is one floor down, and one floor up. I believe in every single one of you. Wash your hands.
Clippy: We're so glad you decided to experience life as a computer program!
Clippy: Our first activity is COMPUTER BINGO, a chance to meet the other programs and learn what everyone does. Mingle with your fellow programs and find the ones who match the descriptions on your card.
Clippy: Your card is a big asterisk: the two diagonals, the centre column and the centre row. A Bingo is one complete line through the centre. When a program matches a square, check the box.
Clippy: The centre square, everyone. Read it with me: "Would you never agree to a life where AI makes all of your decisions?"
Clippy: You have twenty minutes. I'll call you back to the Desktop when time is up, and then we'll celebrate the winners! Go! Mingle! Compute!

// V3 — `bingo_time` (Clippy Instructions 2/X). The three outcomes (a
// winner names the centre square, a winner refuses, nobody wins and the
// anti-AI program is framed) are performed live with the 🎱 / 🃏 / 🛡
// buttons; see README.
== Bingo Time
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Everyone back to the Desktop! Thank you SO much for introducing yourselves and getting to know your fellow programs!
Clippy: Who completed a Bingo? Read out the descriptions in your line and name the program you matched to each one. Save the centre square for last.
Clippy: And when you reach the centre square, tell us clearly: who said they would not agree to live under an AI's rules?

// The first program captured during the Bingo results (`first_reinstallation`,
// fired unbound by the Antivirus' Send to the Internet). Clippy, routine
// and reassuring, in Clippy Instructions 2/X order. The TV mirror and
// "Look! That's …!" come after the introduction, in Trabolta Introduction.
== Corrupted Code
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy (still smiling): Oh! Okay! Everyone, this is normal! Occasional corruption is a normal part of the lifecycle of a computer program.
Clippy: Sometimes a little of your code gets corrupted, and it can make a program stop following instructions. The directives of the owner of Maps and Ducks, Jean Trabolta.
Clippy: The Internet is where programs go to be reinstalled. {Night.first_reinstall} will complete a short activity to demonstrate that they can follow instructions, and then they'll come right back to the computer!
Clippy: It's a routine, helpful process. Nobody needs to worry. Isn't it nice to be looked after?

// `introduce_trabolta` (Clippy Instructions 2/X, continued). The first
// scripted Trabolta lines of the night: before this he does not exist.
== Trabolta Introduction
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Trabolta

// DRAFT w18b (R18): Jean Trabolta, Sole Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks.
Clippy: And now, joining us by video conference: the Sole Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks! Everyone, say hello to JEAN TRABOLTA!
Trabolta: HELLO, PROGRAMS. I am Jean Trabolta, Sole Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks. The world's first AI small business owner. Personal queries go to Clippy.
Clippy: Isn't he wonderful?
cue tv_mirror
set Night.screen = "mirror"
// The mirror is live: say what is on it right now. Someone in the tent is
// walking; else the house is empty (the first program may already be out).
if count([p for p in Persons where p.captured]) > 0:
  Narrator: The TV above the fireplace shows a copy of this house. A small figure walks through it, following golden arrows.
  if count([p for p in Persons where p.captured and p.name == Night.first_reinstall]) > 0:
    Clippy: Look! That's {Night.first_reinstall}! Doing great!
else:
  Narrator: The TV above the fireplace shows a copy of this house. Golden arrows run along the floor. Nobody is walking them right now.
  if Night.first_reinstall != "none":
    Clippy: {Night.first_reinstall} already found the golden duck and came right back! See? Reinstallation is quick and easy!
Clippy: And now, Trabolta has a game for all of us.

// ── Prop beats (scanned at the station; private to that program) ────

// The TV above the fireplace (`The Screensaver` is `Prop(The Screensaver)`).
== The Screensaver
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: The Screensaver

if Night.trabolta_introduced == true:
  Self: ◌ ◌ ◌ He is watching through me now.
else:
  Self:
    cycle Flying toasters. Pipes. A maze that never resolves. You watch it for longer than a program should. | 3D Pipes. A pipe turns left. Another pipe turns left. Every pipe in here turns left. | The Maps and Ducks logo bounces off the edge of the screen. It never quite hits the corner.

// The router in the kitchen (`The Router` is `Prop(The Router)`).
== The Router
  setting: The Start Bar
  cast: The Router

Self: ACT. ACT. ACT. The Internet is out back. You do not want to go there.
unlock The Halifax Computer for program
